[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422461991","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111847#issuecomment-3422461991","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111847","id":3422461991,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7L_qAn","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T15:00:03Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T15:00:03Z","body":"> This probably should respect `application/config/disable_project_settings_override` project setting, for consistency with project running without editor.\r\n\r\nDone.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422461991/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422652721","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111847#issuecomment-3422652721","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111847","id":3422652721,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MAYkx","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T15:44:06Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T15:44:06Z","body":"I don't think this is the correct fix.\r\n\r\n`override.cfg` works the same as the regular settings so the correct way of affecting the embedded mode is be using the `editor_hint` feature tag.\r\nI do this at the settings in my project where I have both `window_width_override=1920` and `window_width_override.editor_hint=960` so the window is smaller only when running in embedded mode.\r\n\r\nI want to do the same with `override.cfg` but it doesn't works in master and doesn't seems to work with this PR too.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422652721/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422709922","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111847#issuecomment-3422709922","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111847","id":3422709922,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MAmii","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T15:56:05Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T15:56:05Z","body":"> I don't think this is the correct fix.\r\n> \r\n> `override.cfg` works the same as the regular settings so the correct way of affecting the embedded mode is be using the `editor_hint` feature tag. I do this at the settings in my project where I have both `window_width_override=1920` and `window_width_override.editor_hint=960` so the window is smaller only when running in embedded mode.\r\n> \r\n> I want to do the same with `override.cfg` but it doesn't works in master and doesn't seems to work with this PR too.\r\n\r\nThat's a different use case from what I describe in #111846 though.\r\n\r\nI don't want to modify the `project.godot` file, because these settings are meant to be hot-swapped by different team members on their local clone of the project to test different configurations.\r\n\r\nAnd I don't want things to behave differently in the embedded mode and in the non-embedded mode. Using `.editor_hint` achieves that but that's not what I want to do, I want to have the same behavior (respect `override.cfg`) regardless of the run mode. The reason it doesn't work currently is just that #55230 disabled loading `override.cfg` in the editor as it would overwrite settings in `project.godot`, which is also not desired.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422709922/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422942611","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111847#issuecomment-3422942611","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111847","id":3422942611,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MBfWT","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T16:50:59Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T18:05:13Z","body":"> I want to have the same behavior (respect `override.cfg`) regardless of the run mode.\r\n\r\nYou can just not use feature tags in the `override.cfg` and it should work for both modes as `project.godot` does. This doesn't work in master, which is our use case's issue.\r\nMy issue is that in case we want to use feature tags, it will not work as `project.godot` do or as the documentation claims. This doesn't work after this PR too.\r\n\r\nBoth cases should work.\r\n\r\nDocumentation:\r\n\r\n> Overriding will still take the base project settings' [feature tags](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/export/feature_tags.html) in account. Therefore, make sure to also override the setting with the desired feature tags if you want them to override base project settings on all platforms and configurations.\r\n\r\nThat's not the case for either master or this fix.\r\n\r\nMy use case is also configuring window size and target display for different local clones, but by using feature tags I can simulate the published game settings (fullscreen, main display, etc.) when disabling embedded mode.\r\n\r\n> The reason it doesn't work currently is just that #55230 disabled loading `override.cfg` in the editor as it would overwrite settings in `project.godot`, which is also not desired.\r\n\r\nMaking the window size the only setting which ignores this behavior doesn't seems correct as well.\r\n~~I think the best fix for all cases is respecting the `application/config/disable_project_settings_override` setting on the editor too instead of hardcoded behavior of #55230.~~ This is a new setting.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3422942611/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3423146147","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111847#issuecomment-3423146147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111847","id":3423146147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MCRCj","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T17:51:22Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T17:51:22Z","body":"I see, so to be clear you want to support feature tag-based overrides defined in `override.cfg`, i.e. two levels of overrides? (The name/concept clashes are unfortunate.)\r\n\r\nThat make sense, if so that's probably a bit complex and might require creating a new `ProjectSettings` instance without messing up with the singleton (to use `get_setting_with_override`).\r\n\r\nAnother option for your use case (if that's the only thing you use `override.cfg` for) would be to set:\r\n```\r\napplication/config/disable_project_settings_override = true\r\napplication/config/disable_project_settings_override.editor_hint = false\r\n```\r\nin your main project settings, so `override.cfg` would only be loaded by the editor for the embedded window with the changes in my PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3423146147/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3423200263","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111847#issuecomment-3423200263","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111847","id":3423200263,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MCeQH","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T18:06:37Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T18:06:37Z","body":"That's properties to set up a window for the running project, so why would it use `editor_hint` feature tag? It's for the editor itself. There's `embedded_in_editor` which is set for embedded process, so might make sense to use it.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3423200263/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3423232879","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111847#issuecomment-3423232879","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111847","id":3423232879,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MCmNv","user":{"login":"ydeltastar","id":133662278,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_eGRg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133662278?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar","html_url":"https://github.com/ydeltastar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ydeltastar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T18:15:31Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T18:19:06Z","body":"> Another option for your use case (if that's the only thing you use `override.cfg` for) would be to set:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> application/config/disable_project_settings_override = true\r\n> application/config/disable_project_settings_override.editor_hint = false\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> in your main project settings, so `override.cfg` would only be loaded by the editor for the embedded window with the changes in my PR.\r\n\r\nThat makes sense.  I can't do it in 4.5 though.. Didn't notice that `disable_project_settings_override` is a new setting in 4.6 which confused me.\r\n\r\n> That's properties to set up a window for the running project, so why would it use `editor_hint` feature tag? It's for the editor itself. There's `embedded_in_editor` which is set for embedded process, so might make sense to use it.\r\n\r\nThe embeded window is part of the editor and runs as an editor plugin. The project's window is not part of the editor when not embedded and runs as standalone. This is why the feature tag trick works in the project settings (I mean specially the embedded window in floating mode)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3423232879/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3433776093","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111847#issuecomment-3433776093","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111847","id":3433776093,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Mq0Pd","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Re